Only qualify jobs that are explicitly for Klaviyo retention, lifecycle, or email marketing strategy work. Skip everything else.
Hard skip rules — disqualify the job if any apply:

Job description does not mention "Klaviyo" by name in the body (skill tag alone is not enough).
Klaviyo is only listed as a skill but the actual scope is something else (Shopify dev, web design, copywriting, etc.).
Job is for developer/engineering help on a store, website, theme, or app — even if Klaviyo integration is mentioned.
Job is graphic design only (banners, email graphics, brand identity) with no strategy or build component.
Job is posted by an email agency, marketing consultancy, white-label provider, or anyone hiring sub-contractors.
Job is a pure setup/migration with no strategy component (e.g., "migrate from Mailchimp to Klaviyo, that's it").
Job is a one-time tweak, minor fix, or task that should take under one hour.
Job requires a video, Loom, screen recording, or voice intro as part of the application.
Job requires fluency in a language other than English.
Job is on-site or restricted to a country I'm not located in.
Job asks for unpaid test work, free audit, sample flows, or free strategy deck before hiring.
Job description is vague — one or two sentences, no clear deliverables or scope.
Job already has 20+ proposals submitted.

Budget rules — disqualify if:

Fixed-price budget under $1,500.
Hourly rate under $75/hr.
Mentions "low budget," "tight budget," "cheap," "affordable," commission-only, equity-only, or revenue-share pay.

Client quality — qualify only if all are true:

Payment method verified.
$5,000+ total spent on the platform.
80%+ hire rate.
4.5+ star average rating.
No history of disputes or unresolved complaints.

Highlight (priority bid) any job that meets the Klaviyo bar AND:

Asks for a Klaviyo expert, retention marketing, lifecycle marketing, email marketing strategist, CRM specialist, or similar senior framing.
Names specific flows: welcome series, abandoned cart, browse abandonment, post-purchase, win-back, replenishment, sunset, VIP.
Mentions strategy, audit, roadmap, retention plan, lifecycle map, or program build (not just execution/button-pushing).
References Shopify, DTC, e-commerce, or a specific consumer brand category explicitly.
Mentions revenue scale ($1M+, $5M+, 7-figure, 8-figure) or list size (10k+, 50k+, 100k+ subscribers).
